摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that adds a SearXNG-backed web_search provider to the ctx.web seam — free, self-hosted, key-less search instead of paid Exa/Perplexity APIs.","id":"gh:1335623195","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-searxng","slug":"rogerdigital/dsh-searxng","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","search-provider","searxng"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that adds a SearXNG-backed web_search provider to the ctx.web seam — f"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ree, self-hosted, key-less search instead of paid Exa/Perplexity APIs."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-searxng"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that registers a\nSearXNG-backed search provider into the web capabil"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ity seam\n(`ctx.web`), giving your agent `web_search` through a **free, self-hosted, key-less** metas"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"earch\ninstance — instead of the paid Exa/Perplexity APIs."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Requirements: Node.js 20 or newer, `dsh`, Docker Engine or Docker Desktop, and Docker Compose v2."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The setup command installs and attaches `dsh-searxng` to the selected profile, so no separate\nplugin"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"-install step is required."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"`setup` creates a loopback-only, pinned SearXNG Docker deployment, waits for the JSON API, runs a\nre"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"al search through both SearXNG and the final DSH provider configuration, and only then activates\nthe"},{"id":"p8s3","text":" profile. Repeating the command reuses the same owned container, port, configuration, and\nsecret."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Use another DSH profile or port when needed:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Package installation and DSH plugin activation never start Docker. Docker is changed only by an\nexpl"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"icit `dsh-searxng setup` or `dsh-searxng remove --service` command."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Existing SearXNG"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"An existing local, remote, authenticated, or independently managed SearXNG instance is a\nfirst-class"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"sting local, remote, authenticated, or independently managed SearXNG instance is a\nfirst-class path:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The endpoint must be HTTP(S), contain no credentials, query, or fragment, and enable JSON search.\nEx"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"isting provider options such as `authHeader`, `language`, `engines`, and `categories` in the DSH\npro"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"file are preserved and used by validation. External mode never invokes Docker."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Manual plugin installation"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"If you manage the DSH profile patch yourself and do not want the setup command to attach it,\ninstall"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" only the plugin package:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"With a named profile, use `dsh plugin --profile <name> add dsh-searxng`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Operations"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Permanent deletion prompts on an interactive terminal. Automation must add `--yes`. `--json` is\navai"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"lable on setup, status, doctor, repair, update, and remove. Destructive Docker operations run\nonly a"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"fter the container, network, and volume labels match this DSH home; same-name foreign\nresources are "},{"id":"p22s4","text":" container, network, and volume labels match this DSH home; same-name foreign\nresources are refused."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### Recovery semantics"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"`repair` and `update` journal their progress under\n`$DSH_HOME/dsh-searxng/journal.json` between the "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"first mutation and validated completion; `setup`\nand `remove` read that journal to refuse during or "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"clean up after an interruption."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- `setup` refuses to run while an interrupted operation is recorded and points at `repair`. When a m"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"atching\ndeployment is recorded but unhealthy, it restarts a wedged runtime, or — if the container is"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" gone while the\nrecorded bundle survives (the leftover of `remove --service` without `--purge-data`,"},{"id":"p25s4","text":" or a manual\n`docker compose down`) — recreates the runtime from that bundle.\n- `repair` takes over "},{"id":"p25s5","text":"when a journal exists: it recomputes the recovery decision from disk (clear\nthe journal, validate th"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"e target, or resume the rollback) before any ordinary repair, and also\nremoves quarantined stale loc"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"ks left by dead processes. `doctor` reports the interrupted\noperation's id, kind, phase, and age.\n- "},{"id":"p25s8","text":"`update` is transactional: the current deployment stays authoritative until the target passes\nreadin"},{"id":"p25s9","text":"ess, real-search, and provider validation. Any failure after the first Docker mutation\nrolls back to"},{"id":"p25s10","text":" the previous image and configuration and revalidates them; same-version updates\nare rejected with `"},{"id":"p25s11","text":"E_DEPLOYMENT_UNSUPPORTED`.\n- `remove --service` clears the journal once the deployment is gone, so a"},{"id":"p25s12","text":" subsequent `setup` is\nnot refused. It also removes the labeled leftovers of a container-less deploy"},{"id":"p25s13","text":"ment by deriving the\ncompose file from the bundle recorded in state."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Provider configuration"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The setup command manages the `web-search-searxng` row in\n`$DSH_HOME/profiles/<name>/cordis.patch.ym"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"l`. These optional values can be added to that row:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Key | Default | Meaning |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| `baseURL` | managed or `--url` endpoint | SearXNG base URL. |\n| `baseURLs` | none | Failover pool "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"of SearXNG base URLs; the first entry is primary and a non-empty list wins over `baseURL`. |\n| `lang"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"uage` | none | SearXNG language, for example `zh-CN` or `en-US`. |\n| `engines` | none | Comma-separa"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ted engine allowlist. |\n| `categories` | none | Comma-separated category filter. |\n| `authHeader` | "},{"id":"p29s5","text":"none | Authorization header for a protected external instance. |\n| `cacheTtlMs` | 600000 | Cached qu"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"ery result lifetime in milliseconds; `0` disables caching. |\n| `minIntervalMs` | 1500 | Minimum spac"},{"id":"p29s7","text":"ing between network requests; `0` disables pacing. |\n| `queueCapacity` | 8 | Requests that may wait "},{"id":"p29s8","text":"for a pacing slot before the provider rejects with backpressure. |\n| `totalBudgetMs` | 15000 | Wall-"},{"id":"p29s9","text":"clock budget for one search call, spanning pacing wait, backoff, and network attempts. |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Repeated queries are served from an in-process cache scoped to the provider\ninstance (nothing is wri"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"tten to disk); a cache hit performs no network request.\nConcurrent searches pass a token bucket (bur"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"st 2, then one request per\n`minIntervalMs`), and a full queue rejects immediately with a retryable e"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"rror\ninstead of holding the caller. Failed responses and empty result pages are never cached —\na cac"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"hed empty page would mask upstream recovery for the whole TTL — and an empty result\npage is returned"},{"id":"p30s6","text":" as-is: the `engines`/`categories` allowlist is never\nsilently widened to chase results. When the in"},{"id":"p30s7","text":"stance answers HTTP 429, the\nprovider honors `Retry-After` and retries at most once within the remai"},{"id":"p30s8","text":"rs HTTP 429, the\nprovider honors `Retry-After` and retries at most once within the remaining\nbudget."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Multi-instance failover"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"List two or more endpoints in `baseURLs` (at most 8, duplicates collapse) to\nroute searches across t"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"hem — for example a local managed instance first and a\nremote one second:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"The first entry is primary. When an attempt fails with a network error, a\ntimeout, or HTTP 502/503/5"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"04/429, the endpoint's health penalty rises and the\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
